22:/// Immutable payload sent from a table renderer to the editor-owned overlay host.
23:///
24:/// The table renderer owns only the anchor and the current toolbar payload. The
25:/// editor owns [TableFloatingToolbarOverlayHost], which renders this payload with
26:/// Flutter's system [OverlayPortal]. This keeps the toolbar outside the table
27:/// block's internal [Stack], so it can cross parent bounds and participate in
28:/// overlay hit testing without making renderers manage overlay entries directly.
29:@immutable
30:class TableFloatingToolbarOverlayRequest {
31:  const TableFloatingToolbarOverlayRequest({
32:    required this.owner,
33:    required this.anchorLink,
34:    required this.anchorRect,
35:    required this.visibleTop,
36:    required this.tableBlockId,
37:    required this.blockIndex,
38:    required this.selectionRange,
39:    required this.toolbarBuilder,
40:    this.enabled = true,
41:    this.minWidth = 0,
42:    this.gap = 4,
43:    this.fallbackHeight = 40,
44:  });
45:
46:  /// Opaque identity of the renderer anchor that published this request.
47:  final Object owner;
48:
49:  /// Link followed by the system overlay entry.
50:  final LayerLink anchorLink;
51:
52:  /// Current rect of the table block anchor in the target overlay coordinates.
53:  final Rect anchorRect;
54:
55:  /// Top edge of the visible editor viewport in target overlay coordinates.
56:  final double visibleTop;
57:
58:  /// Active table identity used by hosts/tests to reason about request staleness.
59:  final String tableBlockId;
60:
61:  /// Active table block index in the source document.
62:  final int blockIndex;
63:
64:  /// Current table-cell selection range that the toolbar actions target.
65:  final TableCellRange selectionRange;
66:
67:  /// Builds toolbar chrome. The renderer captures the table action callback here
68:  /// so the overlay host never calls back into renderer state directly.
69:  final TableFloatingToolbarOverlayBuilder toolbarBuilder;
70:
71:  /// Whether this request may be shown. Hosts hide disabled requests.
72:  final bool enabled;
73:
74:  /// Minimum toolbar width, independent from the table block's layout width.
75:  final double minWidth;
76:
77:  /// Gap between the toolbar bottom and the table anchor top.
78:  final double gap;
79:
80:  /// Height used until the overlay measures its real toolbar child.
81:  final double fallbackHeight;
82:}
