3338:/// Wraps a [_BlockRenderer] so that the underlying block widget (and its
3339:/// [_TextSelectionSurface] children, geometry registration, and text-layout
3340:/// cache) stay mounted even when scrolled out of the viewport — but only when
3341:/// [keepAlive] is true. Used to keep the caret block and selection endpoints
3342:/// alive under editor virtualisation, so the caret and selection
3343:/// highlight always paint and the geometry registry always knows their box.
3344:///
3345:/// Also drives incremental rebuild: a block is only re-rendered when its
3346:/// content changed ([blockChanged]) *or* when the selection / caret / IME
3347:/// composition touches it. A pure caret move inside a different block leaves
3348:/// this block's cached child intact, avoiding the inline-span rebuild that
3349:/// would otherwise run for every block on every keystroke.
